3485	// ===========================================================================
3486	// `/home` EXPANSION — which machine are we asking?
3487	// ===========================================================================
3488	/**
3489	 * The two questions the `/home` expansion has to ask, as an interface rather
3490	 * than a `Client` — because the whole defect this seam exists to prevent was
3491	 * asking the WRONG MACHINE.
3492	 *
3493	 * Incident (found by the 2026-07-27 line audit): `/home` is in `UNSAFE_EXACT`
3494	 * (copying it wholesale would overwrite the new server's own accounts) AND in
3495	 * `DEFAULT_PATHS` (`lib/actions-migrate.ts`), so it is in the default selection
3496	 * of every migration. The fix for that — expand `/home` into its per-user
3497	 * subdirectories — enumerated `/home` with `sh(conn, "ls -1 /home")`, and `conn`
3498	 * is the TARGET connection. A freshly-provisioned Nxeon VPS has an empty (or
